{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Audited from the code and checked against real transcripts. **On a real 50-line Claude Code session, all 50 lines now produce an event — zero unaccounted.** Here's everything still knowingly not recorded:\n\n## Content deliberately dropped\n\n**1. Codex `encrypted_content` blocks embedded inside `agent_message` payloads.** The one place capture still *discards* provider-withheld material instead of sealing it. A standalone `reasoning` item is preserved opaquely; an embedded block is only part of a larger line, so keeping it needs either its own event shape or a decision to fold it into a sibling `reasoning` event. The omission is visible — a bare `{type:\"encrypted_content\"}` marker stays in `raw` — but the ciphertext is gone. In the roadmap; this is the honest gap.\n\n**2. Codex `event_msg` of type `agent_message` / `user_message`.** I verified rather than trusted the old comment: the text is byte-identical to its `response_item` twin, and the counts run the right way (1412 `response_item` assistant vs 1359 `event_msg`; 745 vs 579), meaning every `event_msg` has a twin and not the reverse. Nothing is lost by dropping them.\n\n**3. Secrets.** Replaced with placeholders at capture time — the point of the redaction stack, and what you just `allow`ed one exception to.\n\n**4. File *bodies*.** `resolved` holds sha256 + size, never bytes. Roadmap item, wants a size policy before it ships.\n\n## Structurally unreachable\n\n**5. The tail of a repo's *last* session.** The sweep closes the gap on the next session in that repo; if there is no next session, those final lines stay uncaptured. Roadmap.\n\n**6. opencode tool calls that never settle.** Deferred until `completed`/`error`; a session killed mid-tool leaves that part uncaptured forever.\n\n**7. Empty/whitespace-only opencode text and reasoning parts.** Nothing to record.\n\n**8. Anything outside a git repo**, and any repo with `{\"enabled\": false}` in `.cledger.json`. Both deliberate.\n\n**9. Server-side sessions** — Claude Remote/Cowork, codex cloud tasks — and CLIs with no adapter yet. No local transcript exists to read.\n\n## Looks like loss but isn't\n\n`content` is a *normalized* view; `raw.data` is lossless per line. So the thinking-block `signature`, the envelope fields stripped from record kinds, and Claude's top-level `toolUseResult` (present on ~10k lines in my sample, and not in `content.blocks`) all survive in `raw` — your own security finding was located at `raw/data/toolUseResult/newString`, which is the proof.\n\nOne dead guard worth naming: `user`/`assistant` lines lacking `message` or `timestamp` are silently dropped. Zero occurrences across a 45,730-line corpus, so it's defensive rather than a real hole — but it's the only remaining silent drop, and unlike everything else above it wouldn't announce itself. If you want, I can route those through the `unrecognized` path so they'd be preserved raw and drift-warned instead of vanishing.\n\nresult: Audit complete — 4 deliberate content drops (codex embedded ciphertext the only real one, now roadmapped), 5 structural limits, and confirmation that a real transcript now yields 100% line coverage.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"22af6246a95360b0310727583470b47b6dfff17d","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","seq":1064},"id":"ev1-754b0fe5193e0dcfdea11f06ac070e5911eaeb1af92a33eb50828c00c771f5f8","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-05T02:07:20.475Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.222","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunad